  -- Mary A. Lehman / voting-rights  (Season 1 chair 1 -> blank, COMPOSED_CITATION)
  ('251a2047-372b-480e-aa09-231f9a5edeca'::uuid, 'd1792200-1d3b-4955-a0b7-0e6980d7a7b2'::uuid, '86d893a1-c1a2-4bbf-b4e5-69ec43221194'::uuid, '2a18c152-67a0-4380-a381-cb8795110a7c'::uuid, 'Blanked 2026-10-07. 🔴🔴 THE CITED BILL IS NOT ABOUT WHAT THE ROW SAYS IT IS ABOUT. This chair rests on HB1261 (2023), cited as the "Maryland Voting Rights Act". That bill, read from its own mgaleg page in the session the row names, is "Workplace Fraud and Prevailing Wage - Violations - Penalties and Referrals, sponsored by Delegate Valderrama". The member is not among that bill''s sponsors either. A real bill number has been welded to an act name that does not exist -- the citation looks maximally checkable and is false on inspection. 🔑 THE NAME IS THE FABRICATION, NOT THE NUMBER: a reader who trusts the title never opens the bill, and a reader who opens the bill finds a different subject entirely. Every bill this member sponsored or co-sponsored in the 2023, 2024, 2025 and 2026 Regular Sessions was read from mgaleg''s own per-session member record (Members/Details/<slug>?ys=<session>), which is mgaleg''s attribution and so is not subject to the surname twin. ⚠ The member page defaults to the CURRENT session only, so each session was fetched explicitly. Nothing in the cited instrument speaks to this topic, so chair 1 has no basis. The source examined is kept below so the next reader does not re-derive this from scratch. This is a blank, not a deletion: the chair may well be re-researchable from the member''s actual record, and that is an invitation.', ARRAY['https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Members/Details/lehman01?tab=2023RS-legislation']::text[]),
