-- Kriselda Valderrama / housing -- a Season 2 row already exists at 3; blank it IN PLACE.
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning = 'Blanked 2026-10-07. 🔴🔴 THE CITED BILL IS NOT ABOUT WHAT THE ROW SAYS IT IS ABOUT. This chair rests on HB0997 (2026), cited as "Real Property - Short-Term Rentals" regulation. That bill, read from its own mgaleg page in the session the row names, is "State Finance and Procurement - Prevailing Wage Rate - Calculation". The member DOES sponsor that bill number -- which is what makes this so hard to spot: the number checks out, and only the SUBJECT is invented. A real bill number has been welded to an act name that does not exist -- the citation looks maximally checkable and is false on inspection. 🔑 THE NAME IS THE FABRICATION, NOT THE NUMBER: a reader who trusts the title never opens the bill, and a reader who opens the bill finds a different subject entirely. Every bill this member sponsored or co-sponsored in the 2023, 2024, 2025 and 2026 Regular Sessions was read from mgaleg''s own per-session member record (Members/Details/<slug>?ys=<session>), which is mgaleg''s attribution and so is not subject to the surname twin. ⚠ The member page defaults to the CURRENT session only, so each session was fetched explicitly. Nothing in the cited instrument speaks to this topic, so chair 3 has no basis. The source examined is kept below so the next reader does not re-derive this from scratch. This is a blank, not a deletion: the chair may well be re-researchable from the member''s actual record, and that is an invitation.', sources = ARRAY['https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Members/Details/valderrama?tab=2026RS-legislation']::text[], updated_at = now()
 WHERE politician_id = '768ac1cf-a599-4ddb-943c-c985fafb2607'::uuid AND topic_id = '669cac97-66a6-4087-b036-936fbe62efb3'::uuid AND season_id = '86d893a1-c1a2-4bbf-b4e5-69ec43221194';
