-- ── CORRECTING MIGRATION 1897 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- 1897 blanked these eight rows correctly, but its stated evidence overclaimed the window: it
-- said the member page lists "150 bills for the 2025 and 2026 sessions" when a member page
-- shows the CURRENT session only, so that reading covered 2026RS alone. All four sessions have
-- now been read, and one of 1897's own control counts ("Solar" 0) turns out to be an artefact
-- of that single-session window. The blanks stand; the reasoning is corrected in place because
-- it is shown to voters.
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning = 'Blanked 2026-10-07; evidence corrected 2026-10-07 in migration 1898. 🔴🔴 THE REASONING DESCRIBES A REPUBLICAN; THE CITED PAGE SAYS DEMOCRAT. All eight of Steve Johnson''s Season 1 chairs sat at rung 4 and each was reached by calling him a Republican -- "As an Eastern Shore Republican", "As a Republican member". His own cited page, mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Members/Details/johnson01, states "Party Democrat", District 34A, County Harford, Health Committee ("Harford" 15 hits, "Democrat" 1, "Republican" 0, "Eastern Shore" 0). This database records him as a Democrat. ⚠ CORRECTION TO THE FIRST VERSION OF THIS BLANK. It said the page "lists 150 bills for the 2025 and 2026 sessions". THAT WAS WRONG ABOUT THE WINDOW: a member page defaults to the CURRENT session only, so that reading covered 2026RS alone. All four sessions of his term have since been read explicitly (?ys=2023RS/2024RS/2025RS/2026RS -- 117, 118, 123 and 90 sponsorships). The blank stands, and the evidence is now stated correctly: 🔴 THE CLAIMED INSTRUMENT IS NOT HIS. "Priority Preservation" returns 0 across all four sessions. The bill the row describes is real -- HB0460 (2026RS), "Solar Energy - Construction of Generating Stations in Priority Preservation Areas and Study" -- and its co-sponsors include Delegates April Miller and April Rose, both REPUBLICANS. Steve Johnson is not among them. ⚠ AND THE FIRST VERSION''S "Solar 0" WAS ITSELF AN ARTEFACT OF THE ONE-SESSION WINDOW: he has two solar bills, HB0300 (2023RS) "School Buildings - Solar Technology - Solar Panels on Schools" and HB1233 (2025RS) "Community Solar Energy Generating Systems - Subscription Eligibility", both as co-sponsor and both EXPANDING solar -- the opposite of the restrictive siting bill the row attributed to him. 🔴 The other claimed instruments are genuinely absent across all four sessions: "Fair Districts" 0 (the redistricting row), "Scholarship" 0 (the "Opting in on Opportunity Act" school-vouchers row), "Voter" 0 and "Citizenship" 0 (the "SAVE Our Elections Act of 2026" voting-rights row). 🔴 And one claim is contradicted outright: the public-safety row said he was "opposing major police accountability reforms", while he is a CO-SPONSOR of two such bills -- HB0885 (2025RS) and HB0508 (2026RS), both "Public Safety - Police Accountability - Investigation Records". The bills that ARE his are real and unrelated to these chairs: optometry board revisions, physician and midwife parity, interference-of-custody penalties, and a Schedule III scheduling bill. ⚠ ballotpedia.org/Steve_Johnson_(Maryland), the second source on the voting-rights row, returned a page on which every control term scored 0, including both party names; it was NOT READ and nothing is asserted about its contents. A chair must rest on evidence about the person it is shown under, so there is nothing here to keep. The sources examined are kept below.', updated_at = now()
